\N	2025-06-30 15:57:25.635171+03	loading_time_units	hours	Time units to be used for the resource report: hours, days, weeks
\N	2025-06-30 15:57:25.67826+03	plan.administrativeLeadtime	0	Specifies the number of days (value can be decimal) sales orders should be planned ahead of their due date to take into account for an administrative lead time. Default: 0
\N	2025-06-30 15:57:25.69061+03	plan.minimumdelay	3600	Specifies a minimum delivery date increment (in seconds) used by the planning algorithm in its search. Default: 3600
\N	2025-06-30 15:57:25.702991+03	plan.loglevel	0	Controls the verbosity of the planning log file. Accepted values are 0(silent - default), 1 and 2 (verbose)
\N	2025-06-30 15:57:25.729677+03	plan.individualPoolResources	false	When set to true, an operation-resource record with quantity N is interpreted as 'find N member resources of size 1' instead of 'find a member resource with size N'
\N	2025-06-30 15:57:25.7422+03	plan.rotateResources	true	When set to true, the algorithm will better distribute the demand across alternate suboperations instead of using the preferred operation
\N	2025-06-30 15:57:25.749661+03	plan.autoFenceOperations	999	The number of days the solver should wait for a confirmed replenishment before generating a proposed order. Default:999 (wait indefinitely)
\N	2025-06-30 15:57:25.770596+03	plan.fixBrokenSupplyPath	true	Creates item supplier records with Unknown supplier to fix broken supply path. Default is true.
\N	2025-06-30 15:57:25.78267+03	WIP.consume_material	true	Determines whether confirmed manufacturing orders consume material or not. Default is true.
\N	2025-06-30 15:57:25.79488+03	WIP.consume_capacity	true	Determines whether confirmed manufacturing orders, purchase orders and distribution orders consume capacity or not. Default is true.
\N	2025-06-30 15:57:25.80667+03	COMPLETED.consume_material	true	Determines whether completed manufacturing orders and distribution orders consume material or not. Default is true.
\N	2025-06-30 15:57:25.821357+03	excel_duration_in_days	true	Determines whether numbers in duration fields in spreadsheets are considered as days or seconds. Default is true (for days).
\N	2025-06-30 15:58:34.724043+03	forecast.DoubleExponential_maxAlfa	0.6	Maximum smoothing constant.
\N	2025-06-30 15:58:34.771681+03	forecast.DueWithinBucket	middle	Specifies whether forecasted demand is due at the 'start', 'middle' or 'end' of the bucket.
\N	2025-06-30 15:58:34.783592+03	forecast.Horizon_future	365	Specifies the number of days in the future we generate a forecast for.
\N	2025-06-30 15:58:34.795116+03	forecast.Horizon_history	10000	Specifies the number of days in the past we use to compute a statistical forecast.
